one of the worst defenses in the league this season, ranking 26th or worse in three of the five main efficiency measures. Their one bright spot has been the pass rush, which ranks 5th in sack rate. Chase Young has led the way with 8 sacks. Their scheme has been fairly conventional, and the closest thing to a signature is an eight man box rate that ranks 10th lowest in the league.","special":"The Saints have been about average in how often they go for it on fourth down. Their kickers have made 71% of field goals, which is one of the worst in the league. On the roster side, they put an unusually large share of their salary cap into running backs, about 8% of the money on the books.","players":"Tyler Shough has played nearly every snap at quarterback and thrown for 2,173 yards. Chris Olave has been the clear top target with 27% of the looks and 764 receiving yards. The backfield has been a committee led by Kendre Miller and Alvin Kamara. On defense, Carl Granderson leads the team with 8.5 sacks and Julian Blackmon has picked off 2 passes.","coaching":"Kellen Moore is calling the offense as head coach and Brandon Staley is calling the defense. Their offense looks most like the 2023 Chargers under Kellen Moore and the 2024 Raiders. Their defense looks most like the 2023 and 2024 Panthers, both under Ejiro Evero.","trends":"The offense went from 27th in EPA per play in 2025 to 22nd so far this season, a modest improvement. The defense moved from 10th in EPA allowed per play in 2025 to 21st so far this season, a big step back. The biggest change in approach was blitz rate, which went from 26% to 36%.","notes":"The 2026 pages are built from data that nflverse updates every week, so they will keep changing until the season ends. Personnel, formations, coverage and pressure numbers are missing for now because that data is only released after the season."}}